      "title": "Troubleshooting Cache Service Configuration Issues and Environment Variable Drift",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for identifying and resolving common configuration issues in Cache Service, including environment variable misconfigurations, feature flag failures, and stale internal documentation.",
      "content_body": "When a customer reports service unresponsiveness or data mismatches, first verify that all required environment variables are present and correctly set. Feature flag overrides sometimes fail if the underlying base configuration was not properly propagated to all nodes. A frequent cause of these issues is operators following outdated internal documentation or making manual changes that conflict with the managed configuration. To resolve this, compare the running configuration against the source of truth and apply the correct configuration changes. Finally, review and update any relevant internal documentation to prevent recurrence."
